WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.734
-Our next guest is a talented

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.534
actress you know from the

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.934
hit show "Euphoria,"

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:05.200
as well as movies, such as

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.000
"The King of Staten Island"
and "Other People."

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.300
She's currently starring
as Audrey

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.200
in "Little Shop of Horrors,"
which is now playing

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.534
Off-Broadway
at the Westside Theatre.

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.534
Please welcome back to the show
Maude Apatow, everybody.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.334
[ Upbeat tune plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:25.434
♪♪

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:31.434
♪♪

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:32.868
Welcome back, Maude.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:34.801
-Thank you.
-I don't know if you heard.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.234
Taron is very jealous
that you're

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:37.767
in "Little Shop of Horrors,"
and he's not.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.167
Oh, my God.
I didn't hear that.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:41.033
-Yeah, he was just saying this
is one of his dream roles.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.367
Was this -- I know you're
a huge musical theater fan.

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.167
Was this a dream for you?
-Oh, my gosh, yeah.

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:47.801
This was one of the first shows
I ever saw as a kid,

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.667
so I was so --

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:52.667
yeah, it was extra special
for that reason, I think.

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:55.334
-Now, obviously, you're excited.
Was it also --

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:57.434
Were there some nerves
when you first started doing it?

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:59.267
I mean, I know you're
up and running now

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:01.200
and probably very comfortable.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.267
-No, no, there were so,
so many nerves.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.667
Um, still are.
-Okay.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:09.400
-Yeah, I definitely have like
a history of stage fright,

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.667
so this has been

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.667
very challenging for me.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.167
-I mean, it seems interesting
that you were like,

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.367
"I have a history
of stage fright

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:17.701
and I have taken to the stage!"

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:20.567
[ Laughter ]
-No, it's tricky.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.501
It's always been that way,
but I push through.

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.501
-So, like early,
even as a young actor,

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.067
in school productions,
you would have it?

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:28.033
-Yes.
Like, oh, my gosh.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:31.133
There was one time I was like
in the improv group at my school

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:35.100
and I was always so nervous
to do improv.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.734
And my dad came to like
our like final performance.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:42.033
And every time I'd get like
tapped in to go onstage,

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:45.067
I'd instantly run offstage

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.634
[ Laughter ]
for whatever reason I'd make up.

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:48.734
So, I'd be like, "Oh, yeah,
I'm getting a phone call.

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:50.367
[ Laughter ]
I have to -- I have to go."

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.901
And he's like, "Maude,
you have to stay onstage

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.467
for more than 30 seconds.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.133
[ Laughter ]
Like, it's weird."

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:56.968
So, yeah, it's always
been that way.

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:59.334
-Now your dad, Judd Apatow,
obviously, knows a lot

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:02.968
about comedy, about directing,
and I've heard he's come

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:05.367
to see this show nine times.

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:06.767
-He has.
-Now, that is both

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:08.934
very incredibly loving.

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:11.267
Is he only supportive
or does he bring notes?

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.167
-Oh, he definitely brings notes.
-Lotta notes?

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:14.767
[ Laughter ]
-Lots of notes.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.834
We --

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.000
I know.
Everyone in the cast is like,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.167
"Your dad's here again."
I'm like, "Ugh.

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:21.534
Yeah, he is, huh?"

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:24.467
He sits in the same spot.
Like I could see him.

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:27.734
We have monitors backstage,
of the stage,

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:30.167
and I can see his bald spot

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:33.567
[ Laughter ]
in the monitor when he's there.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:36.834
But, yeah, he loves --
He's going to come like

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.033
I think like eight more times

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:38.901
before I finish.
-Really?!

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:40.801
-Yeah, no, he's a super fan.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.267
-That's really sweet.
And then after each show,

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:46.200
like does he always say,
"Good job," first, I hope?

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.601
-Um...

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.901
[ Laughter ]
yes. Yeah, yeah, no.

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:51.968
But he does give me notes.

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:53.267
He's seen it so many times.

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:57.167
He knows like when I'm having
a bummer show, for sure.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:03:00.200
-Your mom, the wonderful actress
Leslie Mann,

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.100
she's different.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.501
It seems like, based on her
Instagram comments we found,

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:08.300
[ Laughter ]
she seemed to be
very consistently positive.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.801
We've tried to circle them
for everybody to see.

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:12.133
Every single photo,
she just puts a bunch of hearts.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.534
[ Awws and laughter ]

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.868
Like the same hearts
every single time.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.033
I mean, this must be so --

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.667
Have you even noticed
that she was doing this?

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:19.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:22.000
-No.
-No. That is the saddest thing

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.701
for a mom, is she's like --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:25.501
It's like, "I'm sorry.
I didn't notice.

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:27.934
I was reading
what strangers said."
-Oh, my God.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.767
-I didn't realize she was
doing the same thing

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:31.901
on every single photo.
-This one is the best one.

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.767
For the record, don't feel bad
because I don't think

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.033
she notices, either.
Here's a photo where she just

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.534
commented twice in a row.

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:39.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.534
-She really loved that one.
-She loved that one.

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:43.434
She was like she commented once,
she was like, "You know what?

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:44.634
Once isn't enough."
-No.

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:47.167
[ Laughter ]
-You have a wonderful costar

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:48.167
in this -- Matt Doyle.

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:49.434
-Yeah.
-He won a Tony last year.

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:51.133
-Yeah, he's amazing.
-It's a very funny show.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.300
It seems like a show
in an intimate theater

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.000
where people are really enjoying
being together

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.234
and laughing together.
Do you guys ever have trouble

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:59.634
not laughing when you're
onstage together?

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.834
-Oh, my God, so much.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:04.133
We just --

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:06.000
At the end
of "Suddenly Seymour,"

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:11.701
we like embrace and then kiss
and then he like dips me down

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:15.334
and we stay kissing
in that dip position

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.434
for as long
as the audience claps,

00:04:17.434 --> 00:04:19.767
[ Laughter ]
but I think we don't get up,

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.767
so then they think
we're still going,

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.834
so they keep clapping
and it sort of just becomes

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:27.434
[ Laughter ]
like really long,
that we're holding this kiss.

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:28.968
And it's a stage kiss, so like

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.167
we're not actually
like making out.

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:33.667
We're kind of just like still

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:34.868
[ Laughter ]
in a kiss.

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.000
And sometimes we kind of talk
through the kiss.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.367
Like we'll be like,
we'll be like,

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:39.601
"That was a pretty good one,
yeah.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.300
They seem like this."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.467
It's always a little awkward,
but I always think that's funny

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:46.300
and then I'll just
start laughing.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.334
-You mentioned, obviously,
this history of stage fright

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:51.133
and getting over your nerves.
You had an incident recently

00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:53.100
in the show where you had
to get over.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.267
-Yeah.
-Did it help or hurt the nerves?

00:04:56.267 --> 00:05:00.734
-Well, I'm always really kind of
in a panic the entire time

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:03.501
and I was running offstage

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:06.701
and I guess my eyes were kind of
adjusting to the light

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:09.667
and I just ran full speed
into the wall.

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:10.801
[ Ohhs ]
-Yeah.

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:12.601
-And --
-Had they just moved it there

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:14.067
or was it there every night?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:15.501
-Oh, it was definitely there
every night.

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.267
-So, not like
new wall situation.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:18.934
-I know. Everyone was like,
"Wait, the same?"

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.934
And I'm like,
"Let's not get into it."

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:23.601
[ Laughter ]
But yeah, and I got
a concussion.

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:24.834
[ Ohhs ]
-Middle of the show?

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:27.767
-Yeah.
-And did you finish that show?

00:05:27.767 --> 00:05:29.834
-I did. It was insane.
-Wow.

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:31.033
-I don't know what I was doing.
-And was your dad like,

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.968
"I feel like something was off"?

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.601
-God, he would've been,
if he was there.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.834
I swear, I was just like

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:38.501
almost crying the rest
of the show.

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:40.367
My eyes were just like --
I was like --

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:42.300
"Okay, but get through it,
get through it, get through it!"

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.968
[ Laughter ]
And then, yeah, after the show,

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:45.567
I think the adrenaline wore off
and I was like,

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:47.367
"I need to go to the hospital."

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.434
[ Laughter ]
But I'm all good now.
It's fine.

00:05:49.434 --> 00:05:50.968
-You're all good
and it really shows

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:54.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
your commitment to the craft.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.501
They all say,
all the reviews said,

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:58.601
"Maude Apatow would run
through a wall for this part."

00:05:58.601 --> 00:05:59.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:01.934
-It's so humiliating.
I posted on my Instagram like,

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:04.067
"I can't come to the show
tonight. I'm so sorry,"

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:06.467
and everyone was like,
"Screw you."

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:08.834
And then I had to post
the next show I missed,

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:13.033
due to an injury.
I felt like

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:15.000
an athlete.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.567
[ Laughter ]
They can't say, "Screw you,"
if you're like --

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:18.501
unless you're like, "The thing
is I ran into a wall,"

00:06:18.501 --> 00:06:19.567
and they're like,
"Well, come on."

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:20.901
I didn't want to get
into specifics.

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:23.267
-Yeah, don't get into specifics.
-It's too embarrassing.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:24.701
-It's so great to see you.
Congrats on the show...

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.133
-Thank you.
-...and thanks for being back.

00:06:26.133 --> 00:06:27.601
[ Cheering and applause ]
-You guys, that's Maude Apatow,

00:06:27.601 --> 00:06:29.000
everybody.
"Little Shop of Horrors"

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.701
is playing now
at the Westside Theatre.

00:06:30.701 --> 00:06:32.300
We'll be right back
with Jessi Klein.

